Z||000008||Robert||07-10-2001||07:08 PM||||My secret for barbequing steak is this.<BR>Get the best steak you can afford, I buy Harris Ranch top sirloin.  <BR>I then marinade it with Durkee “Grill Creations” black peppercorn marinade mix.<BR>It’s sold in Safeway stores in my area, here is a link to their website. <A HREF="http://www.spiceadvice.com/product_guide/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.spiceadvice.com/product_guide/index.html</A> <BR>It only takes about 20 minutes to marinade, so it’s great on weeknights after work.<BR>I grill the steak for about 15 minutes, and serve with sautéed mushrooms. <BR>Add an artichoke and rice, and “presto” the meal is done.  Of course if my wife is home, we also have to have a salad.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
